      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we actually allocate 3.0A to another port, we should downgrade the pd_source_advertise_max ports and send new LPM source caps on the Attached.SNK port.\n\nThe scenario I envision here:\n1. DRP source attached to port 0\n1. EC sets LPM source caps on port 0 for 3A\n1. 3A PD sink attached to port 1\n1. EC allocates 3A to port 1, and generates new LPM source caps.\n1. PD sink on port 1 requests 5V/3A\n1. Power role swap happens on port 0\n1. PDC sends source cap 5V/3A on port 0\n1. Partner on port 0 requests 5V/3A\n\nAt this point we\u0027re oversubscribed our sourcing.\n\nTo avoid this, I think bits set in pd_source_advertise_max should actually allocate 3A.  Whenever a PD sink, non-PD sink, or FRS partner wants 3A, we can downgrade the pd_source_advertise_max port.",
